      "topic_id": "CN_T00_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "CN_T00_1_LO02",
      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "A student computes the transmission time to send a `15 MB` file (`1 MB = 10^6 bytes`, `1 byte = 8 bits`) over a `10 Mbps` link (`1 Mbps = 10^6 bits/s`) as `15 / 10 = 1.5 seconds`. Which critique and corrected transmission time is accurate?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "The calculation `1.5 seconds` is already correct because `M` cancels out `M` and bytes equal bits in networking."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "The student should divide `15` by `8 × 10` (`15 / 80 = 0.1875 seconds`) because bits are larger than bytes."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "The student forgot to convert `15 MB` using `1 MB = 10^3 bytes`, so the true transmission time is `0.012 seconds`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "The student mixed bytes (`MB`) with bits per second (`Mbps`); converting `15 MB` to `120 × 10^6 bits` and dividing by `10 × 10^6 bits/s` gives `12 seconds`."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "D",
      "answer_explanation": "Transmission time equals `Size_in_bits / Rate_in_bits_per_second`. With `1 MB = 10^6 bytes` and `1 byte = 8 bits`, `15 MB = 15 × 10^6 × 8 = 120 × 10^6 bits`. Dividing by `10 × 10^6 bits/s` yields `12 seconds`—8 times longer than the student's `1.5 seconds`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Although `10^6` cancels between `MB` and `Mbps`, `1 byte = 8 bits` does not cancel, so dividing `15 MB` by `10 Mbps` is off by a factor of `8`.",
        "B": "A byte is `8` times *larger* than a bit (`1 B = 8 bit`), so converting bytes to bits multiplies by `8`, increasing transmission time rather than dividing it by `8`.",
        "C": "The SI prefix `M` (mega) stands for `10^6` (million), not `10^3` (kilo = `10^3`)."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "forgot_byte_to_bit_factor",
        "divided_by_8_instead_of_multiplied",
        "mega_vs_kilo_prefix_confusion"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://book.systemsapproach.org/foundation/performance.html#bandwidth-and-latency",
        "https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Units/binary.html",
        "https://www.nist.gov/pml/owm/metric-si-prefixes#Prefixes"
      ],
      "verification_method": "independent_derivation",
