      "answer_explanation": "Per `Systems Approach §5.2.2` and RFC 9293 §3.9.1.2–3.9.1.3, TCP delivers all 10 bytes reliably and in exact order (`\"HELLOWORLD\"`), but does not preserve the 5-byte + 5-byte write boundaries. Reading `\"HELLOWOR\"` then `\"LD\"` (or `\"HELLOWORLD\"` in one read) is completely valid.",
