      "question_family_id": "QF_CN_T07_2_06",
      "concept_id": "CN_C07",
      "topic_id": "CN_T07_2",
      "learning_objective_id": "CN_T07_2_LO01",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "Switch S1 has ports 1, 2, and 3 in one active VLAN and starts with an empty FDB:\n- Initial FDB: `{}`\n- Event: A frame with `src MAC = M1`, `dst MAC = M2` arrives on port 1.\n\nWhat FDB update and forwarding action occur on Switch S1?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Learn M2 -> port 1; forward the frame out port 1 only"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Learn M1 -> port 1; flood the frame to ports 2 and 3"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Learn M1 -> port 2; forward the frame out port 3 only"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Learn nothing yet; drop the frame until M2 transmits"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Switch S1 learns `M1 -> port 1` from the frame's source MAC and ingress port, and because `M2` is absent from the FDB, it floods the frame to ports 2 and 3.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "The switch learns from the source MAC (`M1`) rather than the destination (`M2`), and it never forwards an unknown unicast back out its ingress port.",
        "C": "`M1` arrived on port 1, not port 2, and `M2`'s location is still unknown so Switch S1 cannot send solely to port 3.",
        "D": "A learning switch immediately learns source `M1 -> port 1` and floods the unknown destination `M2` out ports 2 and 3."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "switch_learns_destination_mac_myth",
        "unknown_unicast_dropped_myth"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://docs.kernel.org/networking/bridge.html",
        "https://docs.kernel.org/networking/switchdev.html"
      ],
      "verification_method": "source_cross_check_and_trace",
