        "A": "A student who correctly wraps the carry bit to get 0001 but skips the final complement picks 0001 instead of inverting to 1110.",
        "B": "A student who truncates the 5-bit sum 10000 to 0000 without adding the carry-out, then inverts, gets 1111 instead of 1110.",
        "D": "A student who substitutes bitwise XOR for one's-complement addition computes 1010 XOR 0110 = 1100 rather than adding with end-around carry."
