      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "A learner claims that each signal symbol is one data bit. In an ideal toy link each symbol actually represents exactly two data bits, without coding overhead. The sender emits six symbols in the first interval and four more in the second. How many data bits are represented in total?",
